  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Field Notebook",
    "overview": "AegeanPulse reads like a practitioner's field notebook: warm paper, dark ink, serif headings with a little character, and one teal pen used for whatever matters on the page. The site is editorial before it is promotional. Articles, prices and plain explanations carry the weight; decoration stays out of their way.\n\nDensity is calm. Sections breathe on generous vertical rhythm, content sits in a readable column, and cards are soft paper slips laid on the page rather than glossy tiles. The one deliberate exception is the home hero: a night-dark field of teal-tinted particles that gives the first screen a pulse before the notebook opens.\n\nComponents are soft and approachable. Buttons and inputs are fully rounded, cards have gently curved corners, and interactive surfaces lift a few pixels on hover. Motion is a single quiet gesture — content fades up into place as it scrolls into view — and disappears entirely for visitors who ask for reduced motion.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Warm off-white paper (light) and deep blue-black (dark), both driven by the same token names.",
      "One accent: Aegean Teal for links, buttons, eyebrows, focus rings and selection.",
      "Fraunces serif for every heading; Inter for everything else.",
      "Pill-shaped buttons and inputs; 16px cards; 24px feature panels.",
      "Hairline borders over heavy shadows.",
      "Fade-up-on-scroll as the only ambient motion."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Pen Rule",
        "body": "Teal is the only accent colour. It marks what is clickable or what to read first; it is never used as a large decorative fill outside the hero particles and washed tints.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Token-Only Rule",
        "body": "Components use the semantic tokens (`background`, `surface`, `foreground`, `muted`, `accent`, `border`), never raw hex. Dark mode is a variable swap under `.dark`, so a component written against tokens is correct in both themes without `dark:` variants.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Serif Headline Rule",
